# WHAT THE ARCHIVE CARRIES, AND WHAT BECOMES OF IT.
#
# One row per thing dist/make-dist.sh packs, saying whether
# install/Install-AmiNetXDuo installs it or deliberately does not, and why.
# tools/check-archive-installed.sh reads this file and checks it BOTH WAYS,
# against the staged tree and against the Installer script.  A file that
# reaches the archive without a row here is a FAILURE, not a warning.
#
# THIS FILE IS THE RECORD.  The reason a thing is not installed lives here, in
# the data the gate reads, and nowhere else -- a reason in a document is a
# reason nothing checks.
#
# WHAT IT EXISTS TO CATCH.  anxnet.device was packed into eleven releases and
# installed by none of them.  A machine kept whatever driver it already had
# through every reinstall, and the archive listing looked correct the whole
# time, because the file was in it.  Nothing compared the two lists; there was
# no second list.
#
# WHY A MANIFEST AND NOT A PARSE OF THE INSTALLER
#
#   Install-AmiNetXDuo is 1700 lines of Installer script and what it copies
#   depends on answers: MINPICK swaps S_LIBS to the minimal drawer, DO_ANXNET
#   gates the driver, an (if (exists ...)) gates tls.library and the trust
#   store.  A grep cannot tell a copy that runs from a copy in a branch nobody
#   takes, and a naive parse that got it wrong would be worse than no check --
#   a green light nobody could read.  So the decision is recorded here, once,
#   by a person, and the parse is reduced to the one question a grep CAN
#   answer: does the script still mention the thing this row says installs it.
#   The third direction, that the copy actually lands, is
#   install/test/run-workbench.sh's, on a real Workbench.
#
# ------------------------------------------------------------- the format --
#
#   glob | disposition | presence | via-or-reason
#
# glob          matched against every regular file in the staged tree, path
#               relative to the directory the archive is packed FROM -- so
#               `AmiNetXDuo.info` is the loose drawer icon beside the drawer
#               and `AmiNetXDuo/AmiNetXDuo.info` is the one inside it.
#               `*` does not cross a slash; `**` does.
#
#               FIRST MATCHING ROW WINS, so a narrow row goes ABOVE the wide
#               one it sits inside.  Get that backwards and the narrow row
#               matches nothing, which the stale-row check below reports.
#
# disposition   installed      the installer puts this on the user's disk
#               not-installed  it deliberately does not
#
# presence      always     every archive this tree can build has it, so a row
#                          matching nothing is a stale row -- FAILURE
#               sometimes  a build option or an optional ingredient decides:
#                          the minimal drawer, tls.library, the trust store,
#                          ssh, scp, the profiler
#
# via-or-reason for `installed`: a literal string that must appear in the CODE
#               of install/Install-AmiNetXDuo -- comments are stripped before
#               the search, since the prose in that file names every drawer it
#               ever copied.
#
#               Name the whole `(source ...)`, not the bare variable.  S_EXAM
#               is a substring of S_EXAMICON, so a row saying `S_EXAM` would
#               still pass with its own copyfiles deleted and the icon's left
#               behind; `(source S_EXAM)` names one statement and breaks when
#               that statement goes.
#
#               for `not-installed`: the reason, in a sentence.  Required.
#               A blank one is refused: "not installed", unexplained, is the
#               shape three drawer icons shipped in for eleven releases.
#
# ------------------------------------------------------ the loose top level --

AmiNetXDuo.info                     | not-installed | always    | The archive's OWN drawer icon, unpacked beside the drawer so a download is one object on Workbench rather than a scattering.  The installer creates its own drawer wherever the user asked and gives it AmiNetXDuo/AmiNetXDuo.info; this copy never leaves the download.
AmiNetXDuo/AmiNetXDuo.info          | installed     | always    | (newname "AmiNetXDuo.info")
AmiNetXDuo/Install-AmiNetXDuo       | not-installed | always    | The installer itself.  Nothing installs an installer.
AmiNetXDuo/Install-AmiNetXDuo.info  | not-installed | always    | Its icon, whose default tool is Installer.  Same reason.
AmiNetXDuo/Uninstall-AmiNetXDuo     | installed     | always    | (source S_UNINSTALL)
AmiNetXDuo/Uninstall-AmiNetXDuo.info | installed    | always    | (source S_UNINSTALLICON)
# Modified Installer 2.17; make-dist checks SHA-256 c6dc78f6e95c8b47204150fa3ff8d0e235866851301a5f1f8ddd05d97ba53137 before staging.
AmiNetXDuo/Installer                | installed     | always    | (source S_INSTALLER)
AmiNetXDuo/InstallSameFile          | not-installed | always    | The Installer's file-identity primitive.  It uses dos.library SameLock to distinguish this drawer's library from a byte-identical system copy, runs before anything is written, and has no use after installation.
AmiNetXDuo/Flavours/*               | not-installed | always    | One key=value manifest per stack the Installer offers: build flags, CPU floor, and every file with its size and sha256.  It describes the download for whoever checks it, and has no use on the machine.
AmiNetXDuo/InstallNetProbe          | not-installed | always    | Read-only network-device discovery for the Installer.  It inspects Emu68's device tree, Zorro Autoconfig, PCMCIA identity tuples and UAE's resident device without opening a network device, and has no use after installation.
AmiNetXDuo/InstallWiFi              | not-installed | always    | The Installer's Wi-Fi page: it asks for the network name and passphrase in its own window and writes Wireless.prefs, because Installer logs every askstring answer and the passphrase must not reach the log.  It has no use after installation.

# ------------------------------------------------------------ the software --
#
# C/ IS ONE ROW ON PURPOSE.  The installer copies that drawer wholesale --
# `(source S_C) (dest D_C) (all)` -- so a command that reaches the drawer is
# installed by construction and a per-command row here would assert nothing.
# Whether a command BELONGS in the drawer is a different question with its own
# check one level up: dist/make-dist.sh walks the build's src/tools and refuses
# a binary that is in neither CMDS nor NOT_SHIPPED, which is how iperf was
# caught after being merged and left out of the archive.

AmiNetXDuo/C/fat/*                  | installed     | sometimes | (source S_CFAT)
AmiNetXDuo/C/*                      | installed     | always    | (source S_C)
AmiNetXDuo/Icons/*                  | installed     | always    | (source (tackon S_ICONS
AmiNetXDuo/Earlier/*                | not-installed | always    | The icons 1.0.0-beta1 to 1.0.0-beta8 copied into C:, byte for byte.  The Installer compares C:NetPrefs.info and C:NetMeter.info with them, to remove an earlier release's icons without keeping them in Backup; a match also sends C:.info, which that copy wrote, to Backup before it is removed.  They have no use after installation.
AmiNetXDuo/Libs/fat/*               | not-installed | sometimes | The fat stack, the fourth section 4 offers: the full stack at -O2 for a 68020 or newer.  Answering "Fat, 68020 and up" points S_LIBS here (MINPICK 3), and is the default on Emu68.  Exactly one stack drawer ships to the disk; which ones are left behind is the user's answer, not a defect.
AmiNetXDuo/Libs/minimal/*           | not-installed | sometimes | One of the THREE stacks section 4 offers, and exactly one drawer ships to the disk.  Answering "Minimal, no IPv6/TLS" points S_LIBS here (MINPICK 1, S_LIBSBASE) and the other two are the drawers that are not installed.  Which ones are left behind is the user's answer, not a defect.
AmiNetXDuo/Libs/micro/*             | not-installed | sometimes | The floor stack: minimal again without getaddrinfo/getnameinfo, ancillary data, the less-used public administration vectors, OOB, the route and address-allocation calls and NetX error checking, and with one interface.  Its private status and control vectors remain because the shipped interface tools use them.  Answering "Micro, one interface" points S_LIBS here (MINPICK 2).  The classic resolver, DHCP and raw sockets remain available; this profile is installed exactly like the other two.
AmiNetXDuo/Libs/bsdsocket.library   | installed     | always    | (tackon S_LIBS "bsdsocket.library")
AmiNetXDuo/Libs/usergroup.library   | installed     | always    | (tackon S_LIBS "usergroup.library")
AmiNetXDuo/Libs/tls.library         | installed     | sometimes | (tackon S_LIBS "tls.library")
AmiNetXDuo/Devs/Networks/fat/*      | installed     | sometimes | (source  dev_source)
AmiNetXDuo/Devs/Networks/micro/*    | installed     | sometimes | (source  dev_source)
AmiNetXDuo/Devs/Networks/*          | installed     | always    | (source  dev_source)
AmiNetXDuo/Devs/Internet/certificates | installed   | sometimes | (tackon (tackon S_DEVS "Internet") "certificates")
AmiNetXDuo/Devs/Internet/*          | installed     | always    | (tackon (tackon S_DEVS "Internet") NDB_F)
AmiNetXDuo/Devs/Firmware/*          | installed     | always    | (source (tackon S_FIRMWARE FW_NAME))

# ---------------------------------------------- the documentation drawers --
#
# Their icons are why this file exists.  Docs.info, Examples.info and
# Terminal.info were packed for every release and copied by none: the installer
# copies the CONTENTS of each drawer, and a drawer's icon sits BESIDE the
# drawer rather than inside it, so `(all)` never saw them.  Examples and
# Terminal landed on the user's disk as drawers Workbench does not draw.

AmiNetXDuo/ReadMe                   | installed     | always    | (source S_README)
AmiNetXDuo/ReadMe.info              | installed     | always    | (source S_README)
AmiNetXDuo/Docs/*                   | installed     | always    | (source S_DOCS)
AmiNetXDuo/Docs.info                | not-installed | always    | The icon for the archive's own Docs drawer, and there is no Docs drawer on the installed side to give it to: the installer copies Docs/ CONTENTS straight into the AmiNetXDuo drawer it created, which already has AmiNetXDuo.info.  Installing this would put an icon beside a drawer that does not exist.  Examples.info and Terminal.info ARE installed, because those two drawers do get created.
AmiNetXDuo/Examples/**              | installed     | always    | (source S_EXAM)
AmiNetXDuo/Examples.info            | installed     | always    | (source S_EXAMICON)
AmiNetXDuo/Terminal/*               | installed     | always    | (source S_TERM)
AmiNetXDuo/Terminal.info            | installed     | always    | (source S_TERMICON)

# ------------------------------------------------------ the Wi-Fi supplicant --
#
# A drawer of its own rather than C/, because C/ is copied wholesale and this
# is copied only when the Pi Wi-Fi is selected, and never over an existing
# C:WirelessManager.  The licence goes with it into the AmiNetXDuo drawer.

AmiNetXDuo/Wireless/WirelessManager | installed     | always    | (source S_WM)
AmiNetXDuo/Wireless/WirelessManager-LICENSE | installed | always | (source S_WMLIC)

# ------------------------------------------------------- codesets.library --
#
# LIBS: on 3.0 and up, only when what is there is older or absent; its
# licence and source pointer go to the AmiNetXDuo drawer every time.

AmiNetXDuo/Codesets/codesets.library | installed   | always    | (source CS_SRC)
AmiNetXDuo/Codesets/SOURCE          | installed     | always    | (source (tackon S_CODESETS "SOURCE"))

# --------------------------------------------------------- the Developer --

# External drivers are copied only for their selected card. Complete GPL
# sources remain available offline in the release rather than on system disks.
AmiNetXDuo/PCMCIA/*.device         | installed     | always    | (source PC_SOURCE)
AmiNetXDuo/PCMCIA/pccard.library   | installed     | always    | (source PC_SOURCE)
AmiNetXDuo/PCMCIA/Docs/*           | installed     | always    | (source S_PCMDOCS)
AmiNetXDuo/PCMCIA/README           | installed     | always    | (source (tackon S_PCMCIA "README"))
AmiNetXDuo/PCMCIA/SHA256.json      | not-installed | always    | Release integrity manifest for the unmodified third-party files; checked by the host packer, not needed to run a driver.
AmiNetXDuo/PCMCIA/Sources/*        | not-installed | always    | Complete original corresponding-source archives and build scripts supplied with every binary release to satisfy the GPL without a separate download; keep with the unpacked distribution.
#
# One decision for the drawer and a second for the profiler under it, and both
# are real choices rather than oversights.  Profile first: it sits inside
# Developer/ and the narrower row has to win.

AmiNetXDuo/Developer/Profile/**     | not-installed | sometimes | The sampling profiler and its self-test.  It profiles ANY AmigaOS program, depends on nothing else in this archive, and a network stack has no business putting a developer tool in somebody's C:.  It ships here because a real machine is the only place its answer can come from -- no emulator above a 68020 has a usable cycle model.
AmiNetXDuo/Developer.info           | not-installed | always    | Its drawer is not installed, so neither is its icon.
AmiNetXDuo/Developer/**             | not-installed | always    | Headers and compiler glue for the vectors past the end of the NDK's SFD.  Where an NDK lives is a property of the compiler somebody has, not of this machine, so a fixed destination would be a guess.  They are in the archive to be copied wherever that NDK is.
